    "question": "Mrs. Oaklyn buys handmade rugs at $40 each and sells them at $60 each. If she bought 20 rugs, calculate the profit she will make from selling the rugs.",
    "gold": "400",
    "answer": "Since she buys one rug at $40 and sells it at $60, she makes a profit of $60-$40 = $<<60-40=20>>20\nIf she bought 20 rugs at $40 and sold them at $60 each, she made a profit of 20*$20 = $400\n#### 400"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine Mrs. Oaklyn's profit from selling the rugs, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the rugs.\n2. Calculate the total revenue from selling the rugs.\n3. Subtract the total cost from the total revenue to find the profit.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total cost of the rugs.\nMrs. Oaklyn buys 20 rugs at $40 each.\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost} = 20 \\times 40 = 800\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the total revenue from selling the rugs.\nMrs. Oaklyn sells each rug for $60.\n\\[\n\\text{Total revenue} = 20 \\times 60 = 1200\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Subtract the total cost from the total revenue to find the profit.\n\\[\n\\text{Profit} = \\text{Total revenue} - \\text{Total cost} = 1200 - 800 = 400\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the profit Mrs. Oaklyn will make from selling the rugs is \\(\\boxed{400}\\).",
